  "boundaries": [
    "Exact-base source snapshots and expanded before-fix controls are retained; initial tests stopped at earlier assertions and are not counted as complete case tables.",
    "Literal recursive parameters do not reinterpret private object keys. Raw request IDs, notification ownership and worker snapshot resolution remain unchanged.",
    "Independent oracle compares small hot/unindexed, hot/indexed and sealed/indexed fixtures. Indexed fixtures assert a usable source checkpoint and topic artifact.",
    "Required topic positions are checked independently in row matching and existing column refinement before pagination, including noncontiguous nullable rows. Native default arity zero and AnyOf([]) match-none are preserved.",
    "Raw WebSocket filters convert once at admission and use the shared native row predicate. Query page fields do not truncate live notifications.",
    "Unsupported safe/finalized/pending tags fail explicitly; raw WebSocket latest bounds are unsupported. HTTP latest still uses the captured query head.",
    "Existing typed blockHash byte-array input is retained as an extension; no global dependency decoder or compatibility change is inferred.",
    "No ingestion writes, persisted schema/index format changes, SQL implementation, live sync, remote host access, production data or benchmark. No throughput claim.",
    "Subscription lag/reorg notification behavior, shared query resource policy, dashboard, verified repair and integrated acceptance remain separate."
  ],
